  "title": "Amsterdam",
  "date": "June 6, 2012",
  "date_iso": "2012-06-06",
  "categories": [
    "Europe"
  ],
  "card_excerpt": "Amsterdaaaaaamn… there are a lot of bikes!",
  "hero_image": "IMG_0173.jpg",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "<p>Amsterdam is a helluva town I say. It's the kind of place I'd like to live in one day, or at least visit if I ever have a kid who studies abroad there. Speaking of which, I first visited this fair city when I was in college studying horticulture. Visit the Netherlands and you'll never think of tulips in the same way again!</p>\n<p>Coming from the US, the first thing you'll notice is the superior airport and train system. I mean, would you ever eat a banana while in the subway in New York City? Viva la the simple things in life!</p>"
    },
